hrough structure, process, and outcomes.", "AENOR:AENOR is the Spanish Association for Standardization and Certification, responsible for developing quality standards.", "ISO:ISO is the International Organization for Standardization, which develops and publishes international standards.", "UNE-EN-ISO 9001:2008:UNE-EN-ISO 9001:2008 is a quality management standard that was commonly used before being replaced by UNE-EN-ISO 9001:2015.", "UNE-EN-ISO 9001:2015:UNE-EN-ISO 9001:2015 is the updated quality management standard that became mandatory in 2017.", "DIMENSIONES DE CALIDAD:\"Dimensiones de calidad\" refers to the criteria and various aspects used to evaluate the quality of healthcare services. This concept encompasses multiple dimensions, including structure, process, and outcome dimensions, as well as accessibility, adequacy, and effectiveness. Together, these dimensions provide a comprehensive framework for assessing the overall quality of healthcare delivery.", "ESTRUCTURA:Estructura refers to the characteristics of the environment in which healthcare is provided, including the necessary resources.", "PROCESO:Proceso refers to the utilization of resources in the delivery of healthcare services, which can be related to both patients and organizations.", "RESULTADOS:Resultados refer to the effects of healthcare interventions on individuals or society, including both intermediate and final outcomes.", "CALIDAD SANITARIA:", "EUROPEAN FOUNDATION FOR QUALITY MANAGEMENT:The European Foundation for Quality Management (EFQM) is an organization that provides a model for excellence in management, particularly in healthcare systems.", "JOINT COMMISSION:The Joint Commission is an external committee that evaluates healthcare organizations to ensure they meet certain standards."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}